    measured_interface_limits: { cell: "O", ev: "SPP-40 (2026-09-07) — O: OPEN, first structural evidence on SPP's own data, on the FIRST SPP KEEPER 2026-09-07-spp-1-baseline (bundle spp40_baseline_B; PRECOMMIT-spp-40-2026-09-07.md §3 pushed before the solve; docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-40-2026-09-07.md §2, §7). The SPP-53 N<->S link (3,400 MW, FCITC construction from SPP's own flowgate limits) is LIVE in every year and binds in the measured N->S-dominant direction in two of three: at bound 2023 1,702 h N->S / 275 h S->N, 2024 878 / 897 (a tie — the rule-29(a) 2024 screen's pre-registered direction leg FIRED on that 22-hour margin and the full span was run under owner direction), 2025 1,245 / 373. Link dual ~-6 $/MWh when N->S bound; the model's mean |S-N| zonal spread ~$1 vs the measured $12-17 hub spread (Nebraska-vs-central-Oklahoma two-point spread the two bubbles cannot hold). NOT a verdict on the TTC value, which was NOT moved (rule 14): the 2024 tie is driven by bubble contents (South overnight wind + CC untrapped by the Oklahoma-internal constraints that bind 60-68 % of hours, FINDING-spp-14 §5), not by the pipe's width. Routed to SPP-DESK: FINDING-spp-53 §6 O-1 (asymmetric pair; S->N is live at the symmetric rating) and O-2 (identification width 2,645-11,121 MW); SPP-57 corroborated as the first lever. No other cell moved (rule 28(d)). ||| SPP-57 (2026-09-07, Fable) — STILL O; the THREE-ZONE ARM WAS KILLED at its pre-registered rule-29(a) STOP gate (PRECOMMIT-spp-57-2026-09-07.md §6, pushed at 910fd5b1 before any limit or price was read; FINDING-spp-57-2026-09-07.md §5): an SPP-Oklahoma pocket (OKGE / PSO / GRDA / WFEC; CSWS split by the measured EIA-861 PSO/SWEPCO ratio 0.5216 / 0.5383) in a chain N<->OK<->S, both links rated by the SPP-53 FCITC construction on a three-point spread — N<->OK 6,500 MW (n_s_corridor UNION oklahoma_internal, 26 constituents N->OK-loaded) and OK<->S 6,700 MW (S->OK-loaded, 19 constituents). On the 2025 screen (keeper-2 recipe + topology; 159 s, 5.13 GB) NEITHER LINK IS LIVE: N<->OK at bound 215 h (2.5 % < 5 %), OK<->S 0 h; the S-OK spread sign mismatches (model 0.00 vs measured +11.29); wind re-curtailment 0.00 %; negative-price hours 0 (control 6; measured ~1,000). The union rule pooled western-Oklahoma delivery elements (Gracemont-Anadarko 6,658 h, Cimarron, Woodward) whose binding makes the OKC hub dearer for reasons the hub-pair regression cannot separate from a North->Oklahoma transfer, and the SAME elements identified S->OK on the second link — a double attribution stated in the config comment before the solve and now measured. What the screen's own flows say, reported not re-cut: at the corridor-only 3,400 MW the N<->OK link would sit at/over bound 2,065 h (1,931 N->OK / 134 OK->N — the measured-dominant direction), and at ~3,400 the OK<->S link 622 h (603 S->OK). Full span NOT spent; nothing registered; the topology was NOT landed (solve path restored to the keeper's two zones, byte-identical); the three-zone implementation + the CSWS split + the two new sidecars (rtbm_bc_oklahoma_limits_2026.parquet, actual_lmp_hourly_area_SPP.parquet) + data/raw/eia-861 stay on the branch / in the tree for a re-issue with corridor-only N<->OK (SPP-53's 3,400) and an OK<->S rating from the SPS-tie set (SPP-54/58's object). NOT a keeper candidate (owner asked in-session; answered: no — structure regressed, the keeper's 3,400 MW binding is what the arm lost)." },
